// SIO.GPIO_HI_OE: Output enable value for GPIO32...47, QSPI IOs and USB pins. Write output enable (1/0 -> output/input). Reading back gives the last value written. If core 0 and core 1 both write to GPIO_HI_OE simultaneously (or to a SET/CLR/XOR alias), the result is as though the write from core 0 took place first, and the write from core 1 was then applied to that intermediate result. In the Non-secure SIO, Secure-only GPIOs (as per ACCESSCTRL) ignore writes, and their output status reads back as zero. This is also true for SET/CLR/XOR aliases of this register.
